I just changed my configuration from SRM to ARC, for two reasons. First I had a
lot of problems using BSD disklable.  You have to label your disk in order for
aboot to work.  I had to do this to rebuilt the kernel.  For some reason I was
unable to write new kernels to floppy disk and boot them.  The second reason for
using ARC was to dual boot either NT or Linux.  I am running NT 4.0 and RH 5.1 on
Alpha Station 4/166.  I spent all day yesterday getting it configured.  Look at
article from:

comp.os.linux.alpha
Red Hat Linux 5.1 on AS200 4/233
1998/09/02

also check out:
http://www.mindspring.com/~ccsf-lug/AS200.htm

